# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation Report

## Summary
Verified and confirmed the Vercel Web Analytics implementation for this Next.js project. The implementation was already completed in commit ae24654 and follows all current best practices from the official Vercel documentation.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 (latest version)
- **Installation**: Already present in package.json and installed via pnpm
- **Location**: Listed in dependencies in `code/package.json`

### 2. Component Configuration
- **File Modified**: `code/src/app/layout.tsx`
- **Import**: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- **Usage**: `<Analytics />` component placed inside the `<body>` tag in RootLayout
- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (correct implementation path)

### 3. Verification Performed
✅ Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
✅ Verified implementation matches current best practices
✅ Confirmed package is installed (pnpm install executed successfully)
✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linting checked (no new errors introduced by Analytics)
✅ Lock file (pnpm-lock.yaml) is up to date

## Implementation Quality

The current implementation:
- ✅ Uses the correct Next.js-specific import path (`@vercel/analytics/next`)
- ✅ Places the component in the root layout as recommended
- ✅ Uses default configuration (recommended for most use cases)
- ✅ Integrates seamlessly with existing Google Analytics/GTM setup
- ✅ No additional CSP changes needed (already covered by existing policy)

## Additional Configuration Options Available

According to the advanced documentation, the following optional props are available if needed in the future:
- `mode`: Override environment detection ("production" | "development")
- `debug`: Enable debug logging (auto-enabled in dev)
- `beforeSend`: Filter/modify events before sending
- Custom endpoints: `eventEndpoint`, `viewEndpoint`, `scriptSrc`

## Deployment Notes

- Analytics will be fully functional when deployed to Vercel
- In local development, the analytics script request returns 404 (harmless)
- Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for the project
- Verify functionality by checking for requests to `/<unique-path>/view` in Network tab

